# #4471 contains two date defects

The 412 unique reports merged into #4471 are not one problem. The ticket-system export has
427 rows, including 15 repeated report IDs. Deduplicating by report ID leaves 412 reports.

| Problem | Reports | GitHub issue |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser treats day-first dates as month-first | 379 | Parser reads day-first tenant dates as month-first |
| booking-v3 advertises an MM/DD/YYYY date format to day-first tenants | 33 | booking-v3 gives day-first tenants an MM/DD/YYYY hint |

## Method

Each unique report was classified from the tenant's locale, its booking-form version, and the
report channel. Every deduplicated report in #4471 belongs to exactly one of the two causes.
The original intake tag is only a guess, so it was not used as the final classification.

## Follow-up

The two causes needed separate outcomes. Keeping them merged would have hidden the 33 reports
caused by the booking-v3 hint behind the larger parser defect.

## Engineering update

#4471 closed on 5 October.

- **Parser — fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **booking-v3 hint — won't fix:** booking-v3 was retired.

The parser ticket is closed as completed. The booking-v3 hint ticket is closed as not planned.

